SECURITY_METADATA_OGTITLE:"Discord Security Bug Bounty",SECURITY_METADATA_DESCRIPTION:"As part of our commitment to security, we reward security researchers for reporting security vulnerabilities responsibly to us. Found a security vulnerability? Submit it here.",SECURITY_HERO_CALLOUT:"Learn More",SECURITY_SUBMIT_VULNERABILITY:"Submit a Vulnerability",SECURITY_INTRO_TITLE:"Discord Security Bug Bounty",SECURITY_INTRO_DESCRIPTION:"At Discord, we take privacy and security very seriously. As such, we encourage everyone to participate in our open bug bounty program, which incentivizes researchers and hackers alike to responsibly find, disclose, and help us resolve security vulnerabilities. As with many bug bounties out there, Discord has a fairly straightforward and simple set of rules that help protect both us and those looking to disclose. Thanks for participating and happy bug hunting!",SECURITY_APPROACH_TITLE:"How we approach security issues",
SECURITY_APPROACH_LINE_1:"Discord will not take legal action against users for disclosing vulnerabilities as instructed here.",SECURITY_APPROACH_LINE_2:"Vulnerability reports will always be responded to as fast as possible—usually within 24 hours.",SECURITY_APPROACH_LINE_3:"Based on the validity, severity, and scope of each issue, we'll reward you with awesome shtuff (or just cold, hard cash if you prefer).",SECURITY_RULES_TITLE:"Program Rules",SECURITY_RULES_LINE_1:"Only use and test on accounts and servers you directly own. Testing should never affect other users.",SECURITY_RULES_LINE_2:"Testing should be limited to sites and services that Discord directly operates. We will not accept reports for third-party services or providers that integrate with Discord through our APIs.",
SECURITY_RULES_LINE_3:"Don't perform any actions that could harm the reliability or integrity of our services and data. Some examples of harmful activities that are not permitted under this bounty include: brute forcing, denial of service (DoS), spamming, timing attacks, etc.",SECURITY_RULES_LINE_4:"Don't use scanners or automated tools to find vulnerabilities.",SECURITY_RULES_LINE_5:"No information about issues found should be publicly disclosed or shared until we've completed our investigation and resolution. After confirmation, you are free to document and publish any information about the issues you've found in accordance with Bugcrowd's [public disclosure policy](https://docs.bugcrowd.com/researchers/disclosure/disclosure/).",
SECURITY_RULES_LINE_6:"If a specific class of vulnerability crops up regularly, we may temporarily mark it Out of Scope while we look to make a solution internally before re-allowing that issue. In these cases, we will update the policy and communicate the change to all current researchers along with a rough expected timeline. Once the internal solution is in place, we will update the policy and communicate the re-allowance.",SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_TITLE:"Processing Report Submissions",SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_LINE_1:"We offer rewards for issues which are submitted and resolved through Bugcrowd. We receive the most benefit when security issues are responsibly disclosed through this bug bounty program so that we can remediate these issues while limiting their risk of abuse.",
SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_LINE_2:"We want to reward the hard work of the original researchers for discovering and demonstrating these issues. If an issue is publicly disclosed, such as through DTesters, Reddit, X / Twitter, etc., then we will consider that finding ineligible for a bounty as we should be rewarding the original researcher for responsible disclosure.",SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_LINE_3:"Determining who the original researcher is when there are multiple report submissions in Bugcrowd can be very difficult, especially when we perform program pauses for holidays. In these cases we will use the following criteria to determine the reporter who provided the most value to our program:",SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_SUB_LINE_1:"The report adequately explains the technical issue being described",SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_SUB_LINE_2:"The report allows our teams to fully understand the impact of the finding",
SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_SUB_LINE_3:"The report has the earliest time of submission in Bugcrowd",SECURITY_REPORT_PROCESSING_LINE_4:"In short, we'll do our best to make sure that the researchers who put in the time and effort to responsibly disclose their findings are correctly rewarded! Please help us by responsibly disclosing your findings only through Bugcrowd in order to receive credit for your work.",SECURITY_SPECIAL_TITLE:"Special Vulnerabilities",SECURITY_SPECIAL_SUBTITLE:"These areas have a more granular scope or have particular considerations prior to reporting.",SECURITY_OUT_OF_SCOPE_TITLE:"Out of Scope Vulnerabilities",SECURITY_OUT_OF_SCOPE_SUBTITLE:"When reporting vulnerabilities, please consider (1) attack scenario / exploitability, and (2) security impact of the bug. The following issues are generally considered out of scope (not an exhaustive list):",SECURITY_TEMPORARILY_OUT_OF_SCOPE_TITLE:"Temporarily Out of Scope Vulnerabilities",
SECURITY_SPECIAL_VULNERABILITIES:"Special Vulnerabilities",SECURITY_THIRD_PARTY_MARKETING_CAMPAIGNS:"Third Party Promotional or Marketing Campaigns",SECURITY_THIRD_PARTY_MARKETING_CAMPAIGNS_DESCRIPTION:"Third-party providers and partners are not in scope. Submissions against third-party promotional or marketing campaigns will not be accepted. Reports with a specific campaign that fail to demonstrate significant security impact or financial harm to Discord are not accepted. Reports against Discord features and APIs are generally in scope. Example out of scope issues:",SECURITY_ACTIVITIES_SCOPE_TITLE:"Activities Within the Discord Client",SECURITY_ACTIVITIES_DESCRIPTION:"Activities served by the Discord client may be first or third party services. The following list of first party Activities are in scope as part of the Discord platform:",
SECURITY_ACTIVITIES_EXCLUSIONS:"Any Activity not explicitly defined above is out of scope for this bug bounty program. Additionally the following are out of scope:",SECURITY_ACTIVITIES_PERMITTED_OVERRIDE:"We consider any situation in which a malicious user could steal tokens or credentials belonging to another user without the use of social engineering in the context of an Activity to be in scope for this program.",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_TITLE:"Race Conditions",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_PREAMBLE:"Any vulnerability report which relies on winning a race condition has additional program requirements for its submission to be accepted.",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_START:"Any report involving a race condition must include one of the following:",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_ENTRY_1:"A script which can consistently reproduce the race condition",
SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_ENTRY_1_SUB_1:"We prefer Python or Javascript as scripting language choices, but any reasonable scripting language will be accepted so long as we can understand the network requirements to reproduce the finding",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_ENTRY_2:"A detailed explanation of how the network layer must be set up to reproduce the finding",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_ENTRY_2_SUB_1:"This must include the full HTTP methods and routes in question",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_ENTRY_2_SUB_2:"This must include a description of how the requests are being sequenced",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_LIST_ENTRY_2_SUB_3:"If the race condition depends on the ordering of the requests that must also be specified in the description",
SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_OUTRO_1:"We will not accept reports which depend on particular Burp Suite configurations. Reports must stand on their own with either a script or a detailed description which can be used to reproduce the race condition being represented.",SECURITY_RACE_CONDITIONS_OUTRO_2:"We strongly suggest providing a script for any report involving a race condition to ensure that your report has the appropriate information to reproduce it and can be quickly reviewed by our team.",SECURITY_QUESTS_TITLE:"Quests",SECURITY_QUESTS_1:"We are not interested in client manipulation, scripts, or other methods which allow individual actors to complete a quest. Quests are currently client authoritative by design and we anticipate that there are many ways in which bad actors can game the progression or completion of quests for individual accounts.",
SECURITY_QUESTS_2:"We are interested in any exploit which allows a malicious actor to claim quest rewards at scale, like generating multiple third party product keys.",SECURITY_QUESTS_3:'In general the guidelines when submitting a report regarding a Quest feature should be: "Does this allow a malicious actor to recover more than one reward for the quest at scale?" We do not consider running a script on multiple individual accounts as qualifying for this purpose.',SECURITY_BEST_EFFORT_DEFENSES_TITLE:"Best Effort Defenses",SECURITY_BEST_EFFORT_DEFENSES_SUBTITLE:"Some areas are treated as best-effort protections. Complete compromise of these systems is still in-scope, but bypasses are generally out-of-scope.",SECURITY_THANKS_TITLE:"Special Thanks to:",SECURITY_CONTACT_US:"Contact us!",
SECURITY_PROGRAM_INVITE_INSTRUCTIONS:"Discord operates a bug bounty program in partnership with Bugcrowd. To join our bug bounty program please send an email with your report to [bugbounty@discordapp.com](mailto:bugbounty@discordapp.com). Please send your full report as the body of your email and include your Bugcrowd username if you are already registered - do not send an email asking for an invitation. If accepted, you will receive an email back from Bugcrowd with further instructions on how to create a Bugcrowd account and complete your report submission! Please note that the [bugbounty@discordapp.com](mailto:bugbounty@discordapp.com) email inbox is unattended - for the security team to review your report you must complete Bugcrowd registration and finalize your submission on the Bugcrowd platform.",SECURITY_REFRESH_METADATA_TITLE:"Security Bug Bounty | Discord",
